WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.001
Look at a plant. It has four main parts.

2
00:00:07.221 --> 00:00:10.843
Each part does a different
job. The plant needs all four.

3
00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:15.290
A new plant grows from a seed.
It looks dead, but it is not.

4
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:19.365
A tiny baby plant, and food
for it, are packed inside.

5
00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:21.907
Give it water and warmth, and it wakes up.

6
00:00:22.127 --> 00:00:26.028
A root pushes down first.
It is hidden in the soil.

7
00:00:26.248 --> 00:00:29.777
Then a shoot pushes up, out of
the soil, towards the light.

8
00:00:30.277 --> 00:00:33.946
Here is the whole plant.
Let us start at the bottom.

9
00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:37.695
These are the roots. They hold
the plant steady in the soil.

10
00:00:37.915 --> 00:00:41.166
The roots drink up water
from the soil, like straws.

11
00:00:41.386 --> 00:00:45.844
This is the stem, the tall
stalk. It holds the plant up.

12
00:00:46.064 --> 00:00:49.965
The stem carries the water up,
from the roots to every part.

13
00:00:50.465 --> 00:00:53.391
These are the leaves.
They are flat and green.

14
00:00:53.611 --> 00:00:57.280
Leaves catch sunlight and use
it to make the plant's food.

15
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.190
A plant makes its own food, in
its leaves. It does not eat soil.

16
00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:06.776
This is the flower. It is the
colourful part at the top.

17
00:01:06.996 --> 00:01:10.804
The flower makes seeds, so there
can be new plants next year.

18
00:01:11.024 --> 00:01:14.553
The whole thing is a plant.
The flower is only one part.

19
00:01:15.053 --> 00:01:17.932
A plant needs water and
light to stay alive.

20
00:01:18.152 --> 00:01:20.567
Take away the water, and the plant droops.

21
00:01:20.787 --> 00:01:23.806
Today you will test the
light, with two plants.

22
00:01:24.026 --> 00:01:27.230
One goes by the window. One
goes in a dark cupboard.

23
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.444
Both get water. Only one
thing is different: the light.

24
00:01:31.664 --> 00:01:36.401
In the dark, the plant goes pale
and thin. Water is not enough.

25
00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:41.499
Scientists use tools. A magnifying
glass helps you look closely.

26
00:01:41.719 --> 00:01:44.598
Hold it near your eye,
and move the leaf closer.

27
00:01:44.818 --> 00:01:47.233
Never point it at the sun. It can burn.

28
00:01:47.453 --> 00:01:51.725
Gloves keep soil off your hands.
Wash your hands afterwards anyway.

29
00:01:52.225 --> 00:01:55.801
A ruler or cubes can
measure how tall a plant is.

30
00:01:56.021 --> 00:02:00.572
Stack cubes beside it, one at a
time. Stop when they reach the top.

31
00:02:00.792 --> 00:02:05.018
Count them: one, two, three. The
seedling is three cubes tall.

32
00:02:05.518 --> 00:02:10.719
Roots drink, the stem carries, leaves
make food, the flower makes seeds.

33
00:02:10.939 --> 00:02:13.726
Plants need light and water. Both.

34
00:02:13.946 --> 00:02:18.358
Scientists use tools safely, and
you can measure a plant in cubes.
